   ◇ Ada reflects: she thinks him a dishonest person, because he did not restore to her a silver pencil which she found under a desk in the clerks' room, and because he has not paid her for certain washing which she did for him.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him ungrateful, because he has run away and left her in the lurch.
   ◇ Ada reflects: She thinks him a swindler, because he has swindled her.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks him a man to be distrusted, because he has cheated the plate.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks him a thoughtful, quiet, steady young man, because he was so quiet and steady on the day when they first spoke together.
   ◇ Arthur reflects: He thinks Mrs. Turner a deceitful person, because she pretended to be an honest, hard-working widow, whereas she has turned out to be a thief.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks her honest, because she found a silver pencil and restored it to the office.
   ◇ Mr. Thomas reflects: He thinks him capable, for he is steady and punctual; honest, for he has never detected him in anything dishonest; diligent, for he has never known him to be absent; and tolerably intelligent, for he has understood whatever has been explained to him.

--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (4/6 key facts kept) ---
I pawned the watch to get bread, and the pencil to get medicine for Fred, who is sick.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (6/6 key facts kept) ---
To-day I entered a wrong figure in the ledger. Resolved never to do so again. Resolved never to do so again. Entered the correct total, 6160. Mr. Thomas examined the quarterly ledgers, and found them not finished. Resolved to finish them in future before 10 p.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (5/5 key facts kept) ---
To-day I set Mr. Hale to balance the quarterly ledger; Mrs. Turner told me she had found a silver pencil under a desk; I sharply turned to Mr. Hale and said, "Attend to the ledger, sir"; I examined the quarterly ledgers, and found them not finished; I resolved never to allow the ledgers to remain unfinished; I proceeded to the cash office, and paid the clerks' wages.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that she was walking beside a canal, and saw reflected in the water the face of a dead man.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas: He dreamt that he was walking with his dead wife along an unfrequented road, and that she pointed to a milestone, and said, "That is ten miles from London."

