--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (1/3 key facts kept) ---
I pawned the silver pencil again for ninepence.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald the death of the Princess Royal, and learned that London Princess Louise, the oldest sister of King George, is seriously ill. I also read that Millwall beat Charlton at football by six goals to nil.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
read in The Times the death of Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister, and read also that she had been seriously ill for some months; Princess Louise was the British Princess Royal.
