--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Tuesday, the 6th of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
I was saddened by reading in the evening paper of the death of Princess Louise, and of mutiny aboard the Lucia, and by learning from Sir Arthur Eddington that the world may come to an end.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Tuesday, the 6th of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
1. Resolved to finish my quarterly ledgers before 10 p. 2. Read in the Daily Herald that all Britain mourned Princess Louise, nicknamed “Her Royal Shyness,” who died of heart disease yesterday. 3. Read that mutiny had broken out aboard the submarine depot ship Lucia, at Plymouth. 4. Heard Sir Arthur Eddington, at a meeting of the Mathematical Association, cautiously predict a slow charge of matter into radiation, ending the universe as a ball of that substance. 5. Finished my ledgers before 10. 6. Wrote to Mr. Walter Thomas.
Signature: Arthur Hale.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Tuesday, the 6th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
1. Read in The Times that all Britain mourned Louise, Princess Royal, nicknamed “Her Royal Shyness,” who died yesterday of heart disease.
   ☾ Ada: She dreamt that Fred came home, and that he and she and Bert supped happily together.
   ☾ Arthur (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was promoted to be chief clerk.
   ☾ Mr. Thomas (forgotten by morning): He dreamt that he was walking somewhere, and saw a man hanging himself.

